### 🚀 Mini Ride Booking System API Testing Guide

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

#############################################
# STEP 1: TEST WITHOUT AUTHENTICATION
#############################################

### 1.1 Register a New Passenger (No auth needed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Test Passenger",
  "email": "test.passenger@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "userType": "PASSENGER"
}

### 1.2 Register a New Driver (No auth needed)  
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Test Driver",
  "email": "test.driver@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "userType": "DRIVER"
}

#############################################
# STEP 2: LOGIN TO GET JWT TOKENS
#############################################

### 2.1 Login as Passenger (COPY THE TOKEN FROM RESPONSE!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2.2 Login as Driver (COPY THE TOKEN FROM RESPONSE!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "bob.wilson@example.com", 
  "password": "password123"
}

#############################################
# STEP 3: REPLACE TOKENS BELOW
# After running login above, copy the "token" value 
# and replace YOUR_PASSENGER_TOKEN and YOUR_DRIVER_TOKEN
#############################################

@passengerToken = YOUR_PASSENGER_TOKEN_HERE
@driverToken = YOUR_DRIVER_TOKEN_HERE

#############################################
# STEP 4: PASSENGER ACTIONS (Use passenger token)
#############################################

### 4.1 Request a Ride (Passenger)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/request
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{passengerToken}}

{
  "pickupLocation": "Airport Terminal 1",
  "dropLocation": "Downtown Hotel",
  "rideType": "CAR"
}

### 4.2 Get My Ride History (Passenger)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/history
Authorization: Bearer {{passengerToken}}

### 4.3 Get Ride Details (use ride ID from request above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/1
Authorization: Bearer {{passengerToken}}

#############################################
# STEP 5: DRIVER ACTIONS (Use driver token)
# 
# 📋 RIDE STATUS FLOW:
# REQUESTED → ACCEPTED → IN_PROGRESS → COMPLETED
#     ↓
# REJECTED/CANCELLED
#
# ⚠️  You can only move forward in this flow!
#############################################

### 5.1 View Available Ride Requests (Driver)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/available
Authorization: Bearer {{driverToken}}

### 5.2 Accept a Ride (Driver) - use ride ID from available requests
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/1/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{driverToken}}

### 5.3 Start the Ride (Driver) - change status to IN_PROGRESS
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/1/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{driverToken}}

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

### 5.4 Complete the Ride (Driver)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/1/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{driverToken}}

{
  "status": "COMPLETED"
}

### 5.5 Get My Ride History (Driver)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rides/history
Authorization: Bearer {{driverToken}}

#############################################
# STEP 6: USER MANAGEMENT (Both can use)
#############################################

### 6.1 Get All Drivers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/drivers
Authorization: Bearer {{passengerToken}}

### 6.2 Get Available Drivers Only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/drivers/available
Authorization: Bearer {{passengerToken}}

### 6.3 Update Driver Availability (Driver only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/drivers/2/availability?status=UNAVAILABLE
Authorization: Bearer {{driverToken}}

#############################################
# STEP 7: ALTERNATIVE - Use Pre-loaded Sample Data
# If you don't want to register new users, use these:
#############################################

### Sample Passenger Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Sample Driver Login  
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "bob.wilson@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

# 📝 INSTRUCTIONS:
# 
# 1. 🚀 Start your Spring Boot app in VS Code (Press F5)
# 
# 2. 🧪 Test the endpoints in order:
#    - First run the registration endpoints (Step 1)
#    - Then login to get tokens (Step 2) 
#    - Copy the token values and replace @passengerToken and @driverToken (Step 3)
#    - Test passenger actions (Step 4)
#    - Test driver actions (Step 5)
#
# 3. 🔍 In Swagger UI (http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html):
#    - First test /api/register and /api/login (no auth needed)
#    - Copy the token from login response
#    - Click 🔒 "Authorize" button at top of Swagger UI
#    - Enter: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
#    - Click "Authorize"
#    - Now all other endpoints will work!
#
# 4. 👥 Pre-loaded sample users (password: password123):
#    Passengers: john.doe@example.com, jane.smith@example.com, alice.johnson@example.com
#    Drivers: bob.wilson@example.com, carol.brown@example.com, david.lee@example.com
